From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:14:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: ispif: Power all VFEs for the ISPIF reset

On MSM8996 the ISPIF reset for VFE0 stops completing once VFE1 has
been powered on and off again. Any stream that powers VFE1 (through
VFE1 itself, or through CSID1, whose power-on also powers VFE1) makes
the next VFE0 stream fail:

  qcom-camss a34000.camss: ISPIF for VFE0 reset timeout
  qcom-camss a34000.camss: Failed to power up pipeline: -5

The reset-done bit never shows up in the raw interrupt status, even a
second after the timeout, although the software register part of the
reset has taken effect. Once the failed attempt has let the CAMSS
power domain switch off, the next attempt works, so every other stream
start fails when two cameras on different CSIDs take turns.

ispif_reset() powers only the VFE whose half of the ISPIF it resets.
Power all VFEs for the reset instead. Samsung's GPL kernel for the
Galaxy Tab S3 does the same: msm_ispif_reset_hw() in
drivers/media/platform/msm/camera_v2/ispif/msm_ispif.c enables both
VFE power domains and both VFE clock sets around the ISPIF reset.

Tested on a Galaxy Tab S3 (APQ8096): 40 raw captures alternating
between CSID0/VFE0 and CSID1 or VFE1 all work; without the change every
VFE0 stream after one that used VFE1 failed.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-ispif.c   | 23 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-ispif.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-ispif.c
index 8ced6b7862..379d2f9f1e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-ispif.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-ispif.c
@@ -315,24 +315,33 @@ static int ispif_vfe_reset(struct ispif_device *ispif, u8 vfe_id)
 /*
  * ispif_reset - Trigger reset on ISPIF module and wait to complete
  * @ispif: ISPIF device
+ * @vfe_id: VFE HW module id
  *
  * Return 0 on success or a negative error code otherwise
  */
 static int ispif_reset(struct ispif_device *ispif, u8 vfe_id)
 {
 	struct camss *camss = ispif->camss;
-	struct vfe_device *vfe = &camss->vfe[vfe_id];
-	int ret;
-
-	ret = vfe_power_on(vfe);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	int i, ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * On MSM8996, once VFE1 has been powered on and off again, the reset
+	 * of VFE0's half of the ISPIF does not complete while VFE1 is off.
+	 * Keep all VFEs powered for the reset, as the downstream driver does.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < camss->res->vfe_num; i++) {
+		ret = vfe_power_on(&camss->vfe[i]);
+		if (ret)
+			goto power_off;
+	}
 
 	ret = ispif_vfe_reset(ispif, vfe_id);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_dbg(camss->dev, "ISPIF Reset failed\n");
 
-	vfe_power_off(vfe);
+power_off:
+	while (i--)
+		vfe_power_off(&camss->vfe[i]);
 
 	return ret;
 }
